NAME
     seq - print a sequence of numbers

SYNOPSIS
     seq [-w] [-s SEP] [FIRST [STEP]] LAST

DESCRIPTION
     seq counts from FIRST (1 by default) to LAST in steps of STEP,
     printing one per line.

OPTIONS
     -w        pad with zeroes so that every number is the same width
     -s SEP    put SEP between them instead of a newline

SEE ALSO
     sh(1) arithmetic, bc(1)
